/target
# `oharness-py` builds outside the workspace, so it has its own
# sibling `target/` that the root-level `/target` rule doesn't cover.
crates/oharness-py/target
# The `python-examples/` project creates its own `.venv` on the
# first `uv sync`. `uv.lock` IS committed (standard practice for
# reproducibility); `.venv` and `.python-version` are per-machine.
python-examples/.venv
python-examples/.python-version
Cargo.lock
*.swp
.DS_Store
.lattice/
